{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-sorting-color-energy-table-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:sorting-color-energy-table-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table from prop:sorting-color-energy","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-sorting-color-energy"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"sorting-color-energy-table-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:sorting-color-energy-table-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Data table from prop:sorting-color-energy</em></p>\n<p>Across the six elements of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_3</code>, the colour energy tracks the inversion count exactly, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_{\\mathrm{colour}} = \\mathrm{inv}(\\pi)\\,(q + q^{-1})</code>: each transposition needed to sort <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code> contributes one crossing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i</code> and one unit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q + q^{-1}</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_{\\mathrm{colour}}</code> grows linearly in the number of swaps.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Permutation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{inv}(\\pi)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Crossings</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_{\\mathrm{colour}}</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1,2,3)</code> sorted</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1,3,2)</code> one swap</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q + q^{-1}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,1,3)</code> one swap</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q + q^{-1}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,3,1)</code> two swaps</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2(q + q^{-1})</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3,1,2)</code> two swaps</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_2 \\sigma_1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2(q + q^{-1})</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3,2,1)</code> reverse</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2 \\sigma_1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3(q + q^{-1})</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}
